  "known_local_policies": [
    "Return the original still-present dead minion residence to its death controller hand, retaining physical owner. Original death and corpse credit are not removed and its already captured Deathrattles remain independent.",
    "Both Secret conditions require effective hand space at acceptance. Later reveal reactions can fill that hand; the accepted operation then uses the existing graveyard delivery overflow profile without another minion death.",
    "The shared ordinary reset precedes return reactions. Cheat Death applies its ordinary permanent local cost delta-2 before acquisition listeners. No new minion or Battlecry is created by return.",
    "Only the first consequence that actually moves the same graveyard residence can return that physical card; later original-death queries see it departed. No substitute same-name minion or later death lifetime is selected.",
    "Old local Fireplace uses Bounce for CFM_800. Old SabberStone copies Kodo, but its Cheat Death test explicitly checks the original entity ID. These references are not current official CN evidence; physical identity and exact reaction/control/return ordering remain documented local policies.",
    "Dirty Tricks and Hidden Wisdom gain the same engine-owned hand-space guard following firsthand public full-hand reports. Empty matching deck/fatigue semantics are unchanged. Bargain Bin full-hand policy is outside this correction and remains its previous local policy."
  ]
